WEBVTT

00:05:27.333 --> 00:05:30.934
AG: But by then, Grace knew
that a counter-anchor makes a difference.

00:05:30.958 --> 00:05:32.435
The final agreement often lands

00:05:32.459 --> 00:05:35.351
somewhere near the midpoint
of the first two offers,

00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:36.643
so she countered.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.351
GS: I think I said something like,

00:05:38.375 --> 00:05:43.726
"I'm so excited to work for the team,
I'm super eager to do X, Y and Z,

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.143
but to be honest,

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:48.851
the rate that was communicated

00:05:48.875 --> 00:05:51.518
was much lower than I had expected.

00:05:51.542 --> 00:05:55.226
So I would love to talk more about this."

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.226
AG: This brings us to a second myth
about getting results.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.018
People think they have to ask
for exactly what they want,